nty has a record back to 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years. In 2025, April to May ran 150% of normal on the middle of the grids, then September to October fell to 51%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 46% and June to July at 96% on the middle of the grids. Grid 18509 has a preliminary estimate of 47.2 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
